  "body": "## Final evidence head\n\n`5dbf00de9dd6c38fb66a46b3dd08a4bdf802824e`, tree `2ea80daad0671a3bdac4b07f9d8bab3a65b6eddc`. The 70-path follow-up preserves a second original NDU artifact, its complete independent comparison and the first entry head's own successful CI. All five public entry files and both original locks retain exactly the same blobs as `81fe7b59`.\n\nThe same-source narrowed release-parity result repeats at **9/9 training and 21/21 holdout**, but the separate narrowed policy-training campaign falls from 9/9 to **8/9**: size 64 versus Rust has p99 **2343/1923 = 1.2184087363**, exceeding the unchanged 1.2 gate. Verified-reduction parity's 18/21 count also hides a changed failed-comparison set. All samples, gates and original failures are preserved. Both distinct-code opportunity observations remain negative; their policy cohorts have zero native-policy invocations and do not establish incremental/economic benefit.\n\nThe first entry head passed [both installation jobs](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/actions/runs/42576902057) and [all four CodeQL jobs](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/actions/runs/42576904491), attempt 1. That history is retained without substituting it for this final head's own required gates. Runtime PR112 is separate: its 17 new tests passed, followed by a stale frozen-source-projection failure; it is not selected or deployed by this PR.\n\n## Why\n\nThe final v16 source `6ecd8023615a6e0b2dc269379fb059c656b38b6f` is qualified and integrated, but public main still only exposes the selected v9 installer. The old installer cannot interpret v16's expanded inventory while preserving its executing-source identity checks. Reviewers also need the original success, failure, scope and cost evidence after CI artifacts expire.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add the unchanged 47,762-byte original B source-CI lock as `releases/hia-v16-6ecd802.json` and a byte-identical B installer under a versioned filename. The current v9 lock, helper and shared preflight retain their exact original blobs.\n- Run independent current/v16 public-installation rows, preserving all original fetch/materialize/check, task-input, native-example and installation-manifest gates and the 35-minute limit. Current still uses the real default with no lock override.\n- Retain B's original **19/19** successful workflow cohort and the separate post-integration **22/22** cohort, including original Lean HTTP-504 failures, bounded reruns, conditional skips and the earlier running-state snapshot. PR817/808 integrated the same qualified B commit into the source baselines.\n- Preserve all 28,122 exact-source and 1,796 full-NDU original member streams plus original scalar/controller data, independent readers and scoped reports. Retain actual-main v9 and runtime PR111 Linux-CI observations.\n- Update the six-track review: the bounded narrowed kernel passes 9/9 training and 21/21 holdout performance comparisons, while matched scalar/controller and distinct-code opportunity results do not establish incremental NDU/economic value. The original Agent four-claim task still fails its strict evaluation gate.\n\n## Validation and boundaries\n\nTwo independent static reviews checked the five entry paths, original lock/helper/preflight bytes, YAML, Bash syntax, embedded Python AST, original gate preservation and command argument order. The full publication tree was calculated locally and matched GitHub's created tree exactly: `2ea80daad0671a3bdac4b07f9d8bab3a65b6eddc`. All 303 JSON files parse; all 39 relative document links resolve; all three default-path Git blobs remain unchanged. Artifact readers check original bytes without executing project/native/solver code.\n\nThis PR's own CodeQL and both public installation jobs are required before merge; actual-main installation must be observed afterward. Source CI does not replace those gates. This metadata publication does not activate an online service or select a new default runtime. General Core completeness, general machine correctness, original Agent-delta adoption/provider costs and stable incremental/economic benefit remain **HOLD**.\n\nThe final publication contains 464 changed paths, mostly retained audit evidence; executable-entry changes are limited to the five reviewed paths above. Full source remains on the separately qualified source branches.\n",
